the Senate Intelligence Committee is  preparing for a highly anticipated  hearing this week with former FBI  director James Comey Comey is scheduled  to testify Thursday about his  conversations with President Trump  Intelligence Committee members mark  Warner and Susan Collins spoke with John  Dickerson on Face the Nation yesterday  about the questions they want answered I  want to know what kind of pressure  appropriate inappropriate how many  conversations he had with the president  about this topic did some of these  conversations take place even before the  president was sworn in this will give us  a chance to get his perspective on the  issue of Russian involvement and also on  the issue of collaboration or collusion  what is he seeing what initial judgments  has he made Democratic Senator Joe  Manchin of West Virginia is also on the  Intelligence Committee good morning the  morning or what's the big question that  you have for the FBI director the  question has been asked by West  Virginians is if you knew or if you  thought there was obstruction of justice  why didn't you act on it and what should  the FBI director well we're anxious to  hear this if how in-depth or what he  thought he was suspicious did he came  back after that meeting and he took all  his notes and filed everything properly  what was his concerns and if there was  deeper concerns why wasn't nothing  Senate done in time yeah you're talking  about what happened on Valentine's Day  inside the Oval Office there's the  Attorney General the Vice President  United States and the FBI director the  president Eights asked the Attorney  General and the vice president to leave  and then reportedly says to the FBI  director I hope you can let this go  meaning the whole Russia investigation  does that raise questions what does  raise questions we want to find out what  Comey was thinking at that time if he  thought it was had risen to that level  of obstruction and if it had why hadn't  something been done why didn't he act on  he was - FBI director if not was that  concern basically filed away for what  purpose his director Comey gonna be in  either by himself or by others on any  restrictions as to what he can say no he  will not go above an open source  basically what you're saying or what's  been reported in the public he's not  going as I understand into a classified  Intel will  sometimes an open meeting such as what  you'll see Thursday and then we go into  another classified setting which is  pretty secure is the president trying to  get executive privilege for him and if  he is will it be successful I don't  think so we have not heard that  whatsoever hasn't been brought to the  committee as far as I know the were  there asking for that I know it's been  reported that that might be done if he  tried that what would be your answer I  think it'd be wrong absolutely I want to  go back to the memos that you said your  constituents raise because we know that  you took very copious notes have you or  anybody on the committee seen the memos  and how important are they to this to  this this hearing on Thursday I haven't  seen those memos yet you want to see  them yes we do we want to see all the  memos I will say this our intelligent  committee is made up of 17 of I think of  truly Americans not Democrats  Republicans and Americans they're going  to make decisions based on the Intel  we've been told and we always believe  that the Intel takes you where the for  the facts the facts will take you to the  truth then you make your decision I  don't think any one person whether it's  a homeless person or a person to highest  level of government such as the  president is going to be spared if  something is wrong that's the rule of  law Senator Mark Warner said there's a  lot of smoke but he's seen no smoking  gun is that your position true did you  mom always say if there's a lot of smoke  there must be fire yeah this is it yes  is there ever seen coming there saying a  lot of smoke signals yeah there's a with  that there's a lot of people that we  know were involved in had had some sort  of contact relationships with the  Russians I just you know the Russians  are not our ally they're not in this to  make it a better America they want  people to distrust distrust their  government not to have confidence that's  what their intentions are through their  news media through all the propaganda  everything they do we should get to the  bottom of it Center listen Vladimir  Putin did an interview over the weekend  with another Network said listen this is  nonsense this is foolishness or  something along those lines you all are  really just making all of this up it  didn't happen the way you're saying do  you think we'll really ever get to the  bottom of this well the Intel is very  very pointed in the direct that they  have gotten more involved they became  more involved and they did everything to  become more involved than ever before  but we've been doing and going back in  this raid for the last 30 40 50 years  why do you think the president  refuses to acknowledge that that I  cannot answer that could be the $64,000  question we have to find out I want to  make sure this gets behind us and I've  said this where the b2 Michael Flynn who  we knew when I was on Armed Services  help us prove your innocence  don't make us pull out you're guilty the  president has an agenda it has to do  with health care it has to do with  immigration it has to do with facts  reform it has to do with infrastructure  all of that is he going to get any of  that pass before the 2018 election I  would sure hope so because this country  needs it counts on all of us to act as  Americans what's best for our country  the Democrats Republicans have become so  siloed that if you have a D by your  neighbor and are by your name you're on  the other side you're the enemy I don't  think that's the oath we all take and we  all take the same oath so why can't we  get together and find out how can we  have a tax reform that really works  gets rid of $23 of debt starts paying  that debt down and secures the country  what did you tell the president about  health care in West Virginia I told the  president I said mr. president there's  180 thousand plus West Virginians that  received health care for the first time  under the first time under the  Affordable Care Act they don't know how  they got it they don't know it was a  Democrat initiative they voted  overwhelmingly for you mr. president  they don't know how they got it they  know how they're going to lose and they  know who took it away from be very  careful where you're going don't use the  word repeal what was his response to  that he listened he listened and we're  hoping that he'll work on that and act  with us but you can't repeal something  that basically we're agreeing 50%  pre-existing conditions caps senior  doughnut hole being filled children  keeping 20 we believe on so many things  why would you throw that out and try to  start over we can't get 60 votes but it  looks like a conflict away out of time  it looks like a contact do you believe  yes or no that conflict can be solved  before the 2018 election I believe it  has to be solved charlie if it doesn't  god help America because we can't  continue down this road and you can't go  back to what we have which is nothing  Thank You senator Manchin always good to  have you thank you no it's good to be  with you

